# The styling conformance scene (docs/styling-plan.md): the brand
# accent, the role tier, and the window inset — slice 1's whole surface,
# asserted at the walls the design says hold each piece (D4):
#
#   - `heading` freezes HERE, on every lane, because every platform
#     publishes it to assistive tech — it is the one role with a
#     real-tree observable everywhere.
#   - `destructive` and `prominent` are DECLARED here so every backend's
#     arm runs, and their press semantics are asserted (a role never
#     changes what a button DOES) — but their look has no AX-visible
#     marker on SwiftUI, so the chrome is held by lowering-side gates
#     and screenshots, not by a step pretending to read it.
#   - the INSET is asserted by measurement: expect_inset reads the
#     halved gap between the padding container's outer extent and the
#     offer inside it — RELATIVE, because absolute offers cannot be
#     byte-frozen across platforms (GTK's CSD headerbar sits inside the
#     window's height where macOS's titlebar sits outside it), while
#     the inset is the same number everywhere.
#   - the BRAND accent is requested (the arm runs on every lane; a
#     backend with a stubbed lowering refuses loudly, which is what
#     keeps this scene off a lane until its lowering is real). Its
#     pixels are the captures' business.
#
# No opening settle: the first expect's bounded retry IS the
# scene-ready wait.
expect label#0 "Sections"
expect_ax label#0 "heading/Sections"
expect_inset 0
expect label#1 "ready"
# The caption role's presence proof (styling-plan D4): its LOOK has no
# universal AX observable (GTK alone has a caption role), so the walls
# are each backend arm's own refusal of an unarmed role, and this text.
expect label#2 "captioned"
expect_ax button#0 "button/Delete"
expect_ax button#1 "button/Save"
# A ROLE NEVER CHANGES WHAT A BUTTON DOES: destructive and prominent
# press like any button, and the app's handler is what acts. These two
# clicks are the semantics half of the roles' contract.
click button#0
expect label#1 "deleted"
click button#1
expect label#1 "saved"
